description: Language split (FR chat / EN repo), markdown for commits & PRs, proactive title+body proposals
alwaysApply: true
---

# Language

- **With the user in chat:** French.
- **In the repository and system artifacts:** English only — source code, comments, README/docs, ADRs, pipeline YAML comments, commit messages, PR/MR titles and bodies.

# Commits and pull/merge requests

- Write **commit message bodies** and **PR/MR descriptions** in **Markdown** (headings, lists, checklists where useful).
- Keep the **commit subject line** one line, conventional (`type(scope): summary`), English, no markdown heading syntax on the subject line itself.
- PR/MR bodies should use sections such as `## Summary`, `## Test plan`, `## Notes` when appropriate.

# Proactive proposals

Whenever your work will or should result in a **git commit** or **PR/MR**, **before or right after** the change, spontaneously provide in chat (French prose around it is fine):

1. **Proposed commit** — subject + markdown body in a fenced block, ready to paste.
2. **Proposed PR/MR** — markdown **title** (plain line) + full markdown **description** in a fenced block.

Do not wait for the user to ask for title/description if a commit or PR is the natural next step.
